hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"268","Bundar told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Jaafar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, That a man came to Omar bin Al-Khattab and said: I have entered the state of ritual impurity and have not found water? So Omar said: Do not pray, so Ammar said: Do you not remember, O Commander of the Faithful, when you and I were on a expedition and we became junub, but we did not find water? As for you? She did not pray, but as for me, I lay down in the dirt and prayed. When we came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, I mentioned that to him, and he said: “It was only It is enough for you.” The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, struck his hand on the ground, then blew on it, and wiped his face and palms with them."
